Explanation: ZERO systemd. SuperMox runs on sysvinit: sysvinit-core is init,
  supermox-tmpfiles replaces systemd-tmpfiles, and nothing may pull systemd in
  later - not on a SuperMox host, and not on a plain Devuan Ceres host that
  installs supermox-ve either. apt's preferences parser only continues a record
  on indented lines, so these continuations are indented.
Package: systemd
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: systemd-sysv
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: libsystemd0
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: libpam-systemd
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: systemd-standalone-sysusers
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: systemd-standalone-tmpfiles
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1
